Another way to think of sequences whose elements are sequences is as
@newterm{trees}.  The elements of the sequence are the branches of the tree,
and elements that are themselves sequences are subtrees.  In this edition the
tree is a recursive union of its own: a @code{Leaf} holds one value, and a
@code{Node} holds the sequence of its subtrees.  @ref{Figure 2.6}
shows the structure in @ref{Figure 2.5} viewed as a tree.

@float
@anchor{Figure 2.6}
@ifinfo
